{"id":"08988737-a544-4ab1-99fb-22d67b7c36e3","revision":0,"last_node_id":85,"last_link_id":153,"nodes":[{"id":48,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[-1940,-90],"size":[700,990],"flags":{},"order":0,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"Model Files — Full BF16 Krea 2 Turbo","properties":{},"widgets_values":["## This workflow uses your full BF16 model\n\n**Diffusion model**\n\n- `krea2_turbo_bf16.safetensors`\n- Original download: [krea/Krea-2-Turbo — turbo.safetensors](https://huggingface.co/krea/Krea-2-Turbo/resolve/main/turbo.safetensors)\n- Location: `ComfyUI/models/diffusion_models/`\n- This is the large BF16 model, not the Comfy-Org INT8 ConvRot model.\n\n**Text encoder**\n\n- `qwen3vl_4b_fp8_scaled.safetensors`\n- Location: `ComfyUI/models/text_encoders/`\n\n**VAE**\n\n- `qwen_image_vae.safetensors`\n- Location: `ComfyUI/models/vae/`\n\n**LoRA**\n\n- `snofsKreaV13D.j1nF.safetensors`\n- Location: `ComfyUI/models/loras/`\n\nThe four file selectors are visible on the main subgraph node and inside the subgraph. Double-click the subgraph to inspect the complete pipeline.\n\nThe BF16 diffusion model is approximately 24.5 GiB and may require substantial system-RAM offloading on an 8 GiB GPU."],"color":"#222","bgcolor":"#000"},{"id":49,"type":"ResolutionSelector","pos":[-470,270],"size":[270,190],"flags":{},"order":1,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"aspect_ratio","name":"aspect_ratio","type":"COMBO","widget":{"name":"aspect_ratio"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"megapixels","name":"megapixels","type":"FLOAT","widget":{"name":"megapixels"},"link":null},{"localized_name":"multiple","name":"multiple","type":"INT","widget":{"name":"multiple"},"link":null}],"outputs":[{"localized_name":"width","name":"width","type":"INT","links":[69]},{"localized_name":"height","name":"height","type":"INT","links":[71]}],"properties":{"Node name for S&R":"ResolutionSelector","cnr_id":"comfy-core","ver":"0.25.0"},"widgets_values":["2:3 (Portrait Photo)",1,8]},{"id":50,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[-1200,-90],"size":[700,990],"flags":{},"order":2,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"Source/reference latent interpolation","properties":{},"widgets_values":["## Krea 2 source/reference latent interpolation\n\nThis workflow encodes two images at the same selected resolution and blends their latent representations before Krea samples.\n\n- `ReferenceMixControl 0.0`: source endpoint\n- `ReferenceMixControl 0.5`: equal latent mixture\n- `ReferenceMixControl 1.0`: reference endpoint\n\nUse `InterpolationDenoise 0.30–0.50` initially. Increase it when the midpoint looks like a double exposure and decrease it when Krea drifts too far from both inputs. Similar image dimensions, subject scale and camera framing produce the clearest interpolation.\n\nPrompt enhancement is absent. The displayed final prompt is sent directly to Krea, with optional LoRA trigger text only when LoRA is enabled."],"color":"#222","bgcolor":"#000"},{"id":47,"type":"MarkdownNote","pos":[-1641.4165450774506,993.5977398311848],"size":[690,510],"flags":{},"order":3,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"title":"SNOFS Krea 2 v1.3D LoKr — No Trigger Word","properties":{},"widgets_values":["Download the style LoRAs used in this workflow from [Comfy-Org/Krea-2/loras](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/Krea-2/tree/main/loras). Place the `.safetensors` files in `ComfyUI/models/loras/`.\n\n| LoRA                   | Trigger Words                        | Recommended Strength |\n|------------------------|--------------------------------------|-------|\n| `krea2_darkbrush`      | `monochrome ink wash style`          | `1.0` |\n| `krea2_dotmatrix`      | `monochrome stippling style`         | `1.0` |\n| `krea2_kidsdrawing`    | `naive expressive sketch style`      | `1.0` |\n| `krea2_neondrip`       | `textured abstract style`            | `1.0` |\n| `krea2_rainywindow`    | `rainy window style`                 | `1.0` |\n| `krea2_retroanime`     | `purple retro anime style`           | `1.0` |\n| `krea2_softwatercolor` | `art deco watercolor style`          | `1.0` |\n| `krea2_sunsetblur`     | `ethereal motion blur style`         | `1.0` |\n| `krea2_vintagetarot`   | `vintage tarot style`                | `1.0` |"],"color":"#222","bgcolor":"#000"},{"id":78,"type":"Note","pos":[-86.8838804118342,1963.3173513388308],"size":[760,390],"flags":{},"order":4,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"properties":{},"widgets_values":["HOW TO PROMPT LATENT INTERPOLATION\n\nDescribe the complete final image, not ‘blend these images’. Tell Krea which composition to preserve and what qualities to borrow.\n\nExample: ‘A coherent portrait preserving the source pose and camera framing, gradually adopting the reference person’s silver costume, cool studio lighting and metallic texture.’\n\nThe mix slider changes the starting latent; it is not a precise semantic percentage. Very different images can create hybrids, double structures or unexpected compositions."],"color":"#243447","bgcolor":"#34526f"},{"id":60,"type":"Note","pos":[-1186.652755673672,1632.6763170976951],"size":[695,300],"flags":{},"order":5,"mode":0,"inputs":[],"outputs":[],"properties":{},"widgets_values":["SOURCE / REFERENCE LATENT INTERPOLATION\n\nReferenceMixControl 0.0 starts entirely from the source latent. 1.0 starts entirely from the reference latent. 0.5 is an equal latent mixture.\n\nInterpolationDenoise tells Krea how strongly to redraw that mixture. Start around 0.30–0.50. Low denoise preserves literal blended structure and may look ghosted; higher denoise gives Krea more freedom to resolve the mixture into one coherent scene.\n\nThis is a whole-image morphing experiment, not masked object replacement. Similar framing and composition usually interpolate more gracefully. Lock the seed when comparing mix values."],"color":"#243447","bgcolor":"#34526f"},{"id":52,"type":"PrimitiveInt","pos":[-470,520],"size":[272.0962890625,110],"flags":{},"order":6,"mode":0,"inputs":[{"localized_name":"value","name":"value","type